 "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-328218" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-328218" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-78246" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation.  Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}-85 \\\\ -119\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-78246" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}-85 \\\\ -119\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =17\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =17v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=17v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=17.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}17 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 17\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-78246" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f526ba55a86b955bad199f9b84b7633a4b111c551f0f9c50cba3bb6a6462d012"} {"question" "q-78246" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-78246" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}17 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 17\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}17 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 17\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}17 & 17 \\\\ 17 & 17\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-78246" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}17 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 17\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-159760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation.  Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-159760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=\\frac{1}{4}v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=\\frac{1}{4}.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-159760" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f526ba55a86b955bad199f9b84b7633a4b111c551f0f9c50cba3bb6a6462d012"} {"question" "q-159760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-159760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-159760" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-328222" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A  linear transformation $T$ represents a dilation. Given that $v=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(v)=[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix $T$ of $T?$\n\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-328222" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =4v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=4v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=4.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-328222" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f526ba55a86b955bad199f9b84b7633a4b111c551f0f9c50cba3bb6a6462d012"} {"question" "q-328222" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-328222" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-328222" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-328222" "field" "field-2