rence/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-78253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write $T(v)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}-20 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-60 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we have $T(v)=\\frac{1}{3}v,$ and so the linear transformation $T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k=\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nThe matrix that represents a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}k & 0 \\\\ 0 & k\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-78253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f526ba55a86b955bad199f9b84b7633a4b111c551f0f9c50cba3bb6a6462d012"} {"question" "q-78253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-78253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3} & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\