lete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-12041" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "Dilation with scale factor $\\frac{1}{3}$"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-78302" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents a reflection in the line $y=-x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-78302" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The correct answer is $T=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ Indeed, consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/assets/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nNow, we can find the images of ${i,j}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-j \\\\ {j}^{′} & =T(j)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=-i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/assets/4a83673a409fd2e5d33b0b5f743f57af08cfb27c38e312a636179102c2172b04.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-78302" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f526ba55a86b955bad199f9b84b7633a4b111c551f0f9c50cba3bb6a6462d012"} {"question" "q-78302" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-78302" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-78302" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-78301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents a reflection in the line $y=x?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-78301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The correct answer is $T=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ Indeed, consider the standard basis ${i,j}$ of the Euclidean plane ${R}^{2}$ and the unit square spanned by the vectors, as shown below. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/assets/9e322e6ed1ddb8f1d094633e931cd179b7eb9d6f47acd7c7d0809f113df91b22.png)\n\nNow, we can find the images of ${i,j}$ under $T$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{i}^{′} & =T(i)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=j \\\\ {j}^{′} & =T(j)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=i\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain the following image:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/assets/0e37a258ea833a2d490fc34a34af40a5c7a18f7589f107c6d0ed631b331c8f2a.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-78301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f526ba55a86b955bad199f9b84b7633a4b111c551f0f9c50cba3bb6a6462d012"} {"question" "q-78301" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-78301" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "q-78301" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4beebc66cf2c0c1a07c229c5cdbf634c22adbd4bbafe00d20176cc356e5d812"} {"question" "e-5452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "A linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ represents a dilation. Given that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/assets/bd6574ee05b60919de656a889f8532e5a512b381eae63f7a65f251a7afe72738.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/assets/be73c2a933a6fb99eaa389774a618848bdadd9cafdf0fcd2f6af126b49b87707.png) what is the standard matrix of $\\mathbf{T}?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/example-5452.json" "file_sha256" "a3409de73eaf323aabf20a60e717dc504fb56923c37017094c4bec35d2b0d606"} {"question" "e-5452" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We can write $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v})$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(v) & =[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ 16\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we have $\\mathbf{T}(\\mathbf{v}) = \\dfrac{1}{4}\\mathbf{v},$ we conclude that the linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ is a dilation with scale factor $k = \\dfrac{1}{4}.$\n\nRemember that the matrix representing a dilation of scale factor $k$ is given by\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/assets/4866597a50fbdb530e9275c77f2ca926c932c7cc334635bd05191aaddd510d75.png)\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/assets/962b9458714f9b7f6b17fe2259e140dfabba443d8ecb5b9e2328172ab3f8a1a2.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/example-5452.json" "file_sha256" "a3409de73eaf323aabf20a60e717dc504fb56923c37017094c4bec35d2b0d606"} {"question" "e-5451" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What linear transformation is represented by the matrix\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/assets/0394b5d3a371caf95d5e701c0ffb00894eb685e706d8b70af2149057de0b0cb5.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060608/example-5451.json" "file_sha256" "d6bc098f42d2207bbb5b753c947a4ef38b249f0221b0e43de1ee20a9520d2ec4"} {"question" "e-5451" "field" nil "attrib